  "meta": {
    "title": "Holland vs the Netherlands: What's the Difference? 🇳🇱🌷🤯",
    "description": "Holland and the Netherlands are not the same thing! 🇳🇱 The Netherlands has 12 provinces, and 'Holland' is just two of them: North Holland and South Holland 🌷 They cover about 13% of the country but hold around 38% of the people, including Amsterdam, Rotterdam and The Hague 🏙️ Because the name was used for the whole country for so long, in 2019 the Dutch government decided to stop promoting 'Holland' and use 'the Netherlands' instead 🤯",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "Holland is only 2 of 12 provinces 🤯🇳🇱",
      "Did you know the difference? 👇",
      "Which country name should we explain next? 🗺️"
    ],
